==============================================================================
  [5]  SIGNIFICANCE OF EACH REACTION
==============================================================================

  Each reaction is fixed at its nominal value and the fit repeated.
  The rise in the sum of squared data residuals is compared against the
  chi-square distribution with 2 degrees of freedom (one A factor and
  one activation energy). Critical values: 5.99 at 95%, 9.21 at 99%.
  A reaction that does not raise the residual is not determined by the
  data and should be frozen (Zhang Eqs. 15-16).

      frozen        residual sum      rise    p value   verdict
      none                76.116                        reference
      R1                  79.657     3.541     0.1703   NOT significant, freeze it
      R2                  76.498     0.382     0.8260   NOT significant, freeze it
      R5                  78.138     2.022     0.3638   NOT significant, freeze it
      R4                 115.975    39.859     0.0000   significant
      R3                  92.270    16.154     0.0003   significant

      Recommendation: freeze R1, R2, R5 and re-run. This
      removes parameters the data does not determine and tightens
      the uncertainty on the remaining ones.

==============================================================================
  [6]  PREDICTIVE TEST  (leave one condition out)
==============================================================================

  Each condition is removed from the fit in turn and then predicted.
  This is the only test of predictive capability: the consistency test
  above uses every condition in the fit, so it can only show internal
  agreement. A prediction that fails while the joint fit passes means
  the conditions are being reconciled by parameters rather than agreeing.
  A held-out absorbance condition keeps its path factor at the prior
  (nominal), since nothing else constrains it.

